  "description": "Captures reproduction as a licensing process. In a world wrecked by climate change, a couple who want a child must first host a state assessor for seven days — she lives in their home, stages tests, plays the child they might have — and her professional courtesy never cracks, which is the horror. Parenthood by evaluation, and the evaluator is the only person in the film doing her job well.\n\nIn the near future where parenthood is strictly controlled, a couple's seven-day assessment for the right to have a child unravels into a psychological nightmare.",
